  "briefing": "The Allied advance along the Riviera has been so fast that most German posts give up or fall back. Not this one: a reserve-division company has dug in on a hill above the coast road with pillboxes, wire, mines and an anti-tank gun, and means to stay. An American parachute battalion, with a tank and a self-propelled howitzer in support, is sent to winkle it out.",
